From: Akisaira <akisaira@outlook.com>
Subject: [PATCH] media: iris: keep the device runtime active while reloading
 the firmware

The sys_error_handler reloads the firmware without a runtime PM
reference of its own. iris_core_deinit() takes one and drops it with
pm_runtime_put_sync() once the core is in DEINIT. If the autosuspend
delay has already run out by then, measured from the last interrupt,
the device runtime suspends right there, and iris_pm_suspend() does
nothing because the core is not in INIT. iris_core_init() then powers
the core and boots the firmware while runtime PM considers the device
suspended. The next pm_runtime_resume_and_get() calls iris_pm_resume(),
which powers the core on a second time and tries to warm boot a
firmware that is already running: "Unbalanced enable for IRQ", context
faults from the video stream, "error booting up iris firmware" on every
resume, and the codecs stay unusable until reboot. A handler that runs
late, or an interrupt thread that spends a while in the response
handler before the SYS_ERROR is acted on, is enough. If the delay runs
out during the reload instead, iris_pm_suspend() can try to power
collapse a firmware that is still answering SYS_INIT.

Hold a runtime PM reference across the reload, as iris_open() does
around iris_core_init(), and drop it with autosuspend afterwards. While
runtime PM is disabled for system sleep the resume fails with -EACCES;
retry the reload later then, instead of running it without the
reference.

Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5-5
Origin: local
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
 drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_probe.c | 21 +++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_probe.c b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_probe.c
index b1ac4a87d8..d6d729103f 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_probe.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/qcom/iris/iris_probe.c
@@ -222,8 +222,29 @@ static void iris_sys_error_handler(struct work_struct *work)
 {
 	struct iris_core *core =
 			container_of(work, struct iris_core, sys_error_handler.work);
+	int ret;
+
+	/*
+	 * Keep the device runtime active across the reload, as iris_open()
+	 * does around iris_core_init(). Otherwise the put in
+	 * iris_core_deinit() can runtime suspend the core while it is in
+	 * DEINIT, which does nothing, and the reloaded core then runs while
+	 * runtime PM considers it suspended.
+	 */
+	ret = pm_runtime_resume_and_get(core->dev);
+	if (ret < 0) {
+		/* Runtime PM is disabled during system sleep: retry later. */
+		if (ret == -EACCES)
+			schedule_delayed_work(&core->sys_error_handler,
+					      msecs_to_jiffies(HW_RESPONSE_TIMEOUT_VALUE));
+		else
+			dev_err(core->dev, "cannot resume to reload the firmware: %d\n", ret);
+		return;
+	}
 
 	iris_core_recover(core);
+
+	pm_runtime_put_autosuspend(core->dev);
 }
 
 static int iris_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
